\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {6}{\ignorespaces Histograms that show the distribution and median of calibration RMSE in the Monte-Carlo simulation that simulates $2000$ sensor calibrations with semi-synthetic data. (Left:) Rotation error. The ground truth rotations have been sampled uniformly across Euler angles. (Right:) Position error. The ground truth position vectors $\boldsymbol  {p} = [p_x, p_y, p_z]$ have been sampled uniformly across the interval $ p_x, p_y, p_z \in [-0.5, 0.5]$~m.}}{8}{figure.caption.6}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:histograms}{{6}{8}{Histograms that show the distribution and median of calibration RMSE in the Monte-Carlo simulation that simulates $2000$ sensor calibrations with semi-synthetic data. (Left:) Rotation error. The ground truth rotations have been sampled uniformly across Euler angles. (Right:) Position error. The ground truth position vectors $\vec {p} = [p_x, p_y, p_z]$ have been sampled uniformly across the interval $ p_x, p_y, p_z \in [-0.5, 0.5]$~m}{figure.caption.6}{}}
